hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"85","[AI-translation] Ubaidullah bin Abdullah bin Utbah se riwayat hai: Ke Waleed bin Abdul Malik ne Umar bin Abdul Aziz (Rahimahullah) ko khat likha jis mein unhen hukm diya ke wo apni taraf se Madinah ke fuqaha se namaz khauf ke bare mein poochen. To Umar bin Abdul Aziz ne un ke fuqaha ke paas [qasid] bheja takeh un se poochen. [Rawi ne] kaha: To Ubaidullah bin Abdullah bin Utbah aaye, jabke qaum [fuqaha] un se ikhtilaf kar chuki thi. Phir unhon ne kaha: Chhodo jo ye kehte hain. Abdullah bin Abbas (Raziyallahu anhuma) ne mujhe bayan kiya ke Rasulullah (Sallallahu alaihi wasallam) ne 'logon ko namaz khauf padhai; Aap ne un mein se ek giroh ko ek rakat padhai, phir wo dushman ke samne ho gaye. Phir doosra giroh aaya, phir unhon ne Aap ke sath doosri rakat padhi. Phir Rasulullah (Sallallahu alaihi wasallam) baithe, tashahhud padha, aur salam phera.' To Rasulullah (Sallallahu alaihi wasallam) ke liye do rakat thin, aur logon ke liye [har ek ke liye] ek rakat."
